      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T08:48:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because microdroid gki requires not only kernel but also initrd. I tried merging modules (zram, zsmalloc) into the normal initrd, but that caused normal microdroid to load the modules, which is unexpected and not good.\n\nAre there any better ways to selectively load kernel modules only for GKI?",
      "parentUuid": "5b5bd672_617e2828",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "2665217ad61bfa763b026780e2209d866bacec41",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08023b20_b20fb5da",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T17:06:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are several options.\n\nOption 1. Add a new bootconfig like `androidboot.load_modules\u003d[true|false]` and let init respect it. Note that we already have `androidboot.load_modules_parallel`. Then we can use the same initrd across gki and microdroid kernels.\n\nOption 2. Add initrd to this struct. \n\nOption 3. Remove this (`kernel`) property and let `gki` select both kernel and initrd.\n\nOption 4. Use `devices.len() \u003e 0` or `vendor.isSome()` as an indicator to use gki and the initrd with modules in it.",
      "parentUuid": "cfab8a14_fa2cfe2a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 28
      },
